  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sukhdev vs State on 12 December, 2017 Author: Sabina Bench: Sabina In The High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Revision No. 342/2004. Sukhdev S/o Anop Gurjar, Resident of Bardiya (Nareda Road), Baran, Police Station Kotwali Baran (Rajasthan) (At present confined in Distt. Jail, Baran) Versus The State of Rajasthan Through Pp. For Petitioner : Shri J.S. Chauhan For State : Shri R.R. Gurjar, P.P. Hon'Ble Mrs. Justice Sabina Judgment / Order 12/12/2017",
    "facts": "Petitioner has faced trial in Criminal Case No.259/1996 pending in the Court of Chief Judicial Magistrate, Baran.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner has submitted that as per the prosecution case petitioner was found in possession of adulterated milk. Occurrence in the present case is of the year 1996. Petitioner is facing criminal proceedings since the year 1996. Learned counsel has submitted that he does not challenge the conviction of the petitioner as ordered by the courts below but has submitted that the sentence of the petitioner qua imprisonment be reduced to the period already undergone by him. Petitioner is not a previous convict and is the sole bread earner of his family. In support of his arguments, learned counsel has placed reliance on the judgment of this court in Loonaram Vs. The State of Rajasthan WLN (UC) 1977, 571 and on the judgments of the Punjab and Haryana High Court in the case of Bharat Lal Vs. The State of Haryana 1993(2) FAC Cases 65, Mahabir Parashad Vs. The State of Haryana 1993(2) FAC Cases 83 and Anil Kumar Vs. State of Haryana 2015(2) FAC 381.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner has submitted that as per the prosecution case petitioner was found in possession of adulterated milk. Occurrence in the present case is of the year 1996. Petitioner is facing criminal proceedings since the year 1996. Learned counsel has submitted that he does not challenge the conviction of the petitioner as ordered by the courts below but has submitted that the sentence of the petitioner qua imprisonment be reduced to the period already undergone by him. Petitioner is not a previous convict and is the sole bread earner of his family. In support of his arguments, learned counsel has placed reliance on the judgment of this court in Loonaram Vs. The State of Rajasthan WLN (UC) 1977, 571 and on the judgments of the Punjab and Haryana High Court in the case of Bharat Lal Vs. The State of Haryana 1993(2) FAC Cases 65, Mahabir Parashad Vs. The State of Haryana 1993(2) FAC Cases 83 and Anil Kumar Vs. State of Haryana 2015(2) FAC 381.",
